From 50c10c1c47410ac45bacd2c943f385b1e850ca9a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: useraccessdenied <useraccessdenied@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 04:08:35 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 14/28] watchdog: qcom: mark an already-armed watchdog as
 running at probe

When the bootloader leaves the apps watchdog enabled, tell the watchdog core (WDOG_HW_RUNNING) so it keeps petting it until userspace opens the device. Without it a slow boot (e.g. a KASAN/lockdep kernel) is reset by the bootloader's watchdog before init runs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/watchdog/qcom-wdt.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/watchdog/qcom-wdt.c b/drivers/watchdog/qcom-wdt.c
index 49bd04841..c533737a6 100644
--- a/drivers/watchdog/qcom-wdt.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/qcom-wdt.c
@@ -333,6 +333,14 @@ static int qcom_wdt_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		set_bit(WDOG_HW_RUNNING, &wdt->wdd.status);
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * The bootloader (ABL on the realme GT Neo 2) leaves the watchdog armed. Tell the core so that
+	 * it keeps petting it from here on (watchdog.handle_boot_enabled) until userspace takes over;
+	 * otherwise a slow boot, e.g. a KASAN/lockdep kernel, gets reset before init runs.
+	 */
+	if (readl(wdt_addr(wdt, WDT_EN)) & QCOM_WDT_ENABLE)
+		set_bit(WDOG_HW_RUNNING, &wdt->wdd.status);
+
 	ret = devm_watchdog_register_device(dev, &wdt->wdd);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
